+  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_5": "The Analyser reveals genetics, the Gene Pool turns organisms into Raw DNA, and the Incubator and Acclimatiser handle reagent production and environmental tolerance. Each has its own focused Ponder scene.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.header": "Sampling genes with the Isolator",
+  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_1": "The Isolator takes a genetic individual and samples one active or inactive allele into an Empty Sequencer.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_2": "The live interface exposes the organism, sequencer, enzyme charge and ethanol tank separately. The machine can consume the specimen during extraction, so keep valuable breeding stock backed up.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.header": "Decoding genes with the Sequencer",
+  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_1": "The Sequencer accepts unsequenced genetic material and progressively identifies the allele stored in it.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_2": "Fluorescent Dye provides the sequencing charge. The live readout fills with decoded bases while progress is retained on the sequence itself.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_3": "When sequencing completes, the discovered gene is recorded for the owner and the Empty Sequencer can be recovered for another sample.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.header": "Charging serums with the Polymeriser",
+  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_1": "The Polymeriser turns a serum or serum array into a reusable genetic tool by adding charges, up to sixteen charges.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_2": "Its two horizontal tanks are Polymerising Bacteria and Raw DNA. Fluid demand scales with the number of genes in the serum array.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_3": "A charged Gold Nugget is optional: supplying one accelerates polymerisation rather than changing the result.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.header": "Applying a serum with the Inoculator",
+  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_1": "The Inoculator applies the genes stored in a charged serum or serum array to a compatible genetic individual.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_2": "Vector Bacteria is the carrier fluid. Successful processing returns the modified organism and removes one charge from the serum.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.header": "High-throughput gene application with the Splicer",
+  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_1": "The Splicer is the aggressive alternative to the Inoculator: it works with serum arrays and processes organisms much faster at a much higher power cost.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_2": "Unlike the Inoculator, its application path does not require a Vector Bacteria tank. Use it when throughput matters more than efficiency.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.header": "Revealing genetics with the Analyser",
+  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_1": "The Analyser identifies hidden information on an unanalysed genetic individual or sequence and records the discovery for its owner.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_2": "DNA Dye is consumed as a charged laboratory reagent. Analysed results can then be understood by Binnie's database and genetics tools instead of remaining opaque.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.header": "Extracting Raw DNA in the Gene Pool",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.text_1": "The Gene Pool is the destructive route through the laboratory: it consumes a genetic individual to produce Raw DNA fluid.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.text_2": "Ethanol feeds the input tank and Enzyme supplies the reagent charge. The organism itself is not returned, so use expendable stock.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.header": "Culturing laboratory reagents in the Incubator",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_1": "The Incubator is a continuous culture machine rather than a single timed recipe. Reagent and fluid combinations are attempted while it has power.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_2": "Growth Medium with water produces Growth Medium fluid.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_3": "Wheat in Growth Medium cultures ordinary Bacteria.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_4": "From there, Sugar can make Enzyme; White Dye produces Polymerising Bacteria and Blaze Powder produces Vector Bacteria. The same machine also matures bee larvae in Growth Medium.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.header": "Adapting organisms with the Acclimatiser",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_1": "The Acclimatiser changes an organism's tolerance alleles in place. It repeatedly attempts a valid adjustment while supplied with power and reagents.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_2": "Acid and alkaline fertilisers steer pH tolerance in opposite directions.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_3": "Heat and cold reagents adjust temperature tolerance, while Water and Sand adjust humidity tolerance. The machine never emits a separate finished genome: the individual itself changes.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.header": "Specialising a Forestry Alveary",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_1": "Binnie's Alveary components replace ordinary exterior Alveary blocks. The Forestry multiblock keeps its normal 3×3×3 body and slab cap; only the chosen wall positions change.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_2": "The Mutator consumes mutagen items and multiplies mutation chance, with the resulting modifier capped rather than growing without limit.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_3": "The Frame Housing accepts one Forestry hive frame, contributes that frame's modifiers, and wears the frame while the Alveary runs.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_4": "The Rain Shield lets rain-sensitive bees continue working through bad weather.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_5": "The Lighting block supplies artificial daylight for species that would otherwise stop without suitable light or sky conditions.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_6": "The Stimulator accepts a compatible circuit board and applies its configured bee modifiers while the component is powered.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_7": "The Hatchery can produce larvae from a healthy working queen and stores the resulting larvae internally.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_8": "The Transmission block accepts FE and distributes it to Alveary components that require power, giving powered upgrades a shared supply point.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.header": "Breeding Binnie's genetic flowers",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_1": "Binnie's flowers are genetic organisms. Two flowers can look alike while carrying different active and inactive alleles, so parent choice matters.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_2": "Pollen carries a flower genome. Apply it to another mature flower to pollinate that parent with the donor's genetics.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_3": "Offspring are produced as genetic seeds. Their genomes combine the parents and can contain new inherited traits or mutations, so grow and select the offspring you want to continue breeding.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_4": "Flowerbeds track moisture, acidity, fertility and weedkiller. Use the Soil Meter to inspect the bed, then water or amend the soil instead of guessing what the flower needs.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.header": "Mounting databases on the Lab Stand",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_1": "The Lab Stand is not a processing machine. It is a physical home for Binnie's genetic knowledge databases, keeping frequently used reference tools in the laboratory world.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_2": "Right-click the placed stand with a compatible database to mount it. The mounted item is rendered on the stand instead of disappearing into an invisible inventory.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_3": "Right-click the occupied stand to access the mounted database. Database items can be moved between compatible Lab Stands when you reorganise the laboratory."
 }
